{
  "title": "Transmission-gate mux",
  "group": "Electronics — digital",
  "description": "transmission-gate 2:1 analog mux: SEL toggles the output between a 50 MHz sine and a 25 MHz square",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -173,
        "title": "Transmission-gate mux — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A 2:1 analog mux from two CMOS transmission gates.",
          "SEL (vpulse) and its inverse from inverter MPS/MNS",
          "steer the gates: MNA/MPA pass input VA, a 50 MHz sine",
          "(VA on offset VAO); MNB/MPB pass VB, a 25 MHz square.",
          "Only one gate conducts at a time, so vout (at load CL)",
          "follows VA or VB depending on SEL.",
          "Probes sel, va, vb, vout show the hand-off.",
          "",
          "Set SEL.pw = 5e-08 and re-run: the shorter high",
          "time makes the mux favor one input over the other."
        ]
      }
    ],
